# Exercise 962: Single Static Comparison

Disposition: **EQUIVALENT**. One exercise, four tasks, four equivalent tasks,
zero findings. No fixes.

The author and frozen FIRST JSON/Markdown were hash-bound before comparison.
The author schema was inspected first; its source object was not descended
and source.data was not inspected. No fresh source was opened.

## Task Results

| Task | Piecewise and domain | Zero and graph construction | Author points in FIRST |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| a | Same -1 left, 1 right; zero excluded | Same two horizontal rays and open endpoints (0,-1), (0,1); no point at zero | 4/4 |
| b | Same 2 left, -2 right; zero excluded | Same two horizontal rays and open endpoints (0,2), (0,-2); no point at zero | 4/4 |
| c | Same -x^2 left and x^2 right; all real inputs | Same retained half-parabolas and included origin; odd and increasing | 5/5 |
| d | Same x^2 left and -x^2 right; all real inputs | Same retained half-parabolas and included origin; reflection of c, odd and decreasing | 5/5 |

For a and b the zero treatment is an excluded jump with two open ray
endpoints, not a removable hole or an arbitrarily filled point.
The author's shorter zero_boundary wording is consistent with its explicit
graph_construction fields.

For c and d the author includes zero in its x>=0 branch. FIRST gives a
separate x=0 branch and describes both parent half-parabolas as including
their common vertex, explicitly drawn once. Both representations describe
the same included origin and the same retained branches. No endpoint defect
is present.

All 18 author plotting coordinates are present identically in FIRST's 34
coordinates. Numeric-versus-string serialization was normalized solely for
static pair membership. FIRST's additional 16 points and fuller prose are
accepted detail differences, not reasons to recompute or rerun checks.
The frozen Markdown agrees with the frozen JSON and author on these fields.

Task-id separators, equation prefixes, implicit versus explicit multiplication,
and internal field names are representational differences, not a publisher
schema requirement.

